  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Prove that if $a$ and $b$ are odd integers, then $a^2-b^2$ is divisible by 8.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a^2-b^2=4(m-n)(m+n+1)$, where $a=2m+1$ and $b=2n+1$.\n\nOne of $m-n$ and $m+n+1$ is even, so the difference is divisible by 8.",
      "worked": "Write $a=2m+1$ and $b=2n+1$, where $m,n$ are integers.\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2-b^2&=(a-b)(a+b)\\\\a^2-b^2&=(2m-2n)(2m+2n+2)\\\\a^2-b^2&=4(m-n)(m+n+1).\\end{align*}$$\nThe integers $m-n$ and $m+n$ have the same parity because their difference is $2n$. If $m-n$ is even, the product contains a factor of 8. If $m-n$ is odd, then $m+n$ is odd and $m+n+1$ is even, so the product again contains a factor of 8. Hence $a^2-b^2$ is divisible by 8.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
